render/pixman: map RGB888 and BGR888

The pixman renderer has no 24bpp formats, so it can neither render into
an RGB888 or BGR888 buffer nor sample one, and wl_shm does not offer
them. Some display controllers scan out no 32bpp packed format at all,
only 24bpp.

render/pixel_format.c already describes both (3 bytes per block). Map
them to pixman's r8g8b8 and b8g8r8. pixman packs its 24bpp formats in
host byte order, so they match the DRM formats on little-endian only,
like the 16bpp and 10bpc entries beside them.

Signed-off-by: badgeos
---
diff --git a/render/pixman/pixel_format.c b/render/pixman/pixel_format.c
index c308a2b..1b4af1c 100644
--- a/render/pixman/pixel_format.c
+++ b/render/pixman/pixel_format.c
@@ -72,6 +72,14 @@ static const struct wlr_pixman_pixel_format formats[] = {
 	// Since DRM formats are always little-endian, they don't have an
 	// equivalent on big-endian if their components are spanning across
 	// multiple bytes.
+	{
+		.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_RGB888,
+		.pixman_format = PIXMAN_r8g8b8,
+	},
+	{
+		.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_BGR888,
+		.pixman_format = PIXMAN_b8g8r8,
+	},
 	{
 		.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_RGB565,
 		.pixman_format = PIXMAN_r5g6b5,
